From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:01:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: release thread lock holds at exit, IR
 validate-and-repair, L1-only lookup cache

Covers ml599 and ml612-ml622.

BTCpu64IosReleaseThreadHolds (Module.cpp, exported in libarm64ecfex.def) is
called from wine's pthread_exit_wrapper before the TSD-275 clear, while TEB and
FEX state are still reachable. A thread that died holding a CodeInvalidationMutex
read hold used to wedge the whole app: the writer queues behind the dead reader
and write-priority blocks every later reader, so JIT compilation stops
process-wide. Verify the stamp against CodeInvalidationMutex::IosStampAddress()
and never poke the futex word directly.

RedundantFlagCalculationElimination and RegisterAllocationPass both walked a
block's Previous chain unbounded; validate before mutate and repair from the
forward chain. IRTopologyCheck.h adds a per-pass sweep to name a corrupter.

LookupCache is L1-only, worth 70-100 MB across many threads.

AllocWatch is diagnostic only. Its per-record drain is deliberately gone: it
formatted 512 lines from inside a corruption path and killed the process with
its own format-string text as the exception code. Do not reinstate it.

